cff-version: 1.2.0
title: DiplotypeForge
message: >-
  If you use DiplotypeForge, please cite this software and the simulation-design
  references below.
type: software
authors:
  - name: Society for Immune Polymorphism (SIP)
    website: "https://github.com/societyforimmunepolymorphism"
repository-code: "https://github.com/societyforimmunepolymorphism/DiplotypeForge"
url: "https://github.com/societyforimmunepolymorphism/DiplotypeForge"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible simulation of phased HLA diplotypes from HFX haplotype
  frequencies, including population mixtures, admixture, Hardy-Weinberg
  disequilibrium, and GL String output. A component of the SIP HLA Forge
  initiative.
keywords:
  - HLA
  - KIR
  - immunogenetics
  - population genetics
  - haplotype
  - diplotype
  - simulation
  - HFX
  - GL String
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      16th IHIW: Global analysis of registry HLA haplotypes from 20 million
      individuals
    authors:
      - family-names: Maiers
        given-names: Martin
    journal: International Journal of Immunogenetics
    year: 2012
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Genotype List String: a grammar for describing HLA and KIR genotyping
      results in a text string
    authors:
      - family-names: Milius
        given-names: Robert P.
    journal: Tissue Antigens
    year: 2013
